<title>USA: Great Western sues over &quot;double counting&quot;.</title>
<headline>Great Western sues over &quot;double counting&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>CHATSWORTH, Calif. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Western Financial Corp said it filed suit in Delaware against H.F. Ahmanson and Co over the double counting issue.</p>
<p>Earlier, Ahmanson, which has made a hostile bid for Great Western, said an independent inspector certified more than a majority of Great Western shares voted in favor of a proposal requiring Great Western to hold its annual meeting by May 6.</p>
<p>Great Western has alleged that Ahmanson &quot;double counted&quot; votes on some consent proposals.</p>
<p>&quot;It is now the Court that will decide the outcome of the consents.  Nothing Ahmanson claims can excuse their blatant attempt to double count votes,&quot; Great Western said Monday.</p>
</text>
